bodyText:
The director may commence a proceeding to terminate a limited liability company administratively if the company fails to:

(1) Pay any fees prescribed by law;

(2) File its annual report for a period of two years pursuant to section 428-210;

(3) Appoint and maintain an agent for service of process as required by this part; or

(4) File a statement of a change in the name or business address of the agent as required by this part.
